# Brand package agent guide

Read `README.md` first. This file is the steps; the reasoning is in `docs/brand/principles/` (start with `shared.md`).

## Change a token

1. Edit `packages/brand/<brand>/project/tokens.json` (`orin` or `techworx`). It is the source: Panda reads it, and the Claude design system artifact is published from it.
2. Keep the artifact format. Every family except `type` is `{"tokens": [{name, value, usage}]}`, a list. Colour also has `themes`. Never write a name-to-value map.
3. Names match `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,63}` and are unique across every family except `type`. Give every token a `usage` note that says where it is used.
4. Colour values are hex, `rgb()`, `rgba()`, `hsl()`, `hsla()` or `oklch()` with no function inside, or an alias `"{other-token}"` of an existing colour token. Never use `var()`, `color-mix()` or a named colour (`red`, `transparent`, `currentColor`). Put the primary theme first; a token missing a theme inherits the first theme's value.
5. Run `cd packages/brand && npx vitest run`. It checks the rules above, alias resolution, theme count and text contrast (4.5:1 on the grounds a usage note names).
6. Run `npx oxlint` and `npx oxfmt --check .` in the package, then `just ci` from the repo root before handing off a change that touches Panda.

Why not DTCG: the Claude design system artifact cannot read a name-to-value map (the family shows empty and its entries are lost at the first edit), so the artifact format is the source. A DTCG file would be a generated export for Figma only; there is none yet.

Panda reads these files through `packages/foundations`. Check both Orin themes (dark, light) and both techworx modes (outline, preview) after a colour change. There are no copies: foundations imports the two files directly (`packages/foundations/src/brandFiles.ts`). The old `semantic.json` is kept only as `test/fixtures/semantic.legacy.json`, so the fold test in `test/helpers.ts` can show that no role changed value. Check the generated CSS after a token change by running Panda's `cssgen` for the projects that use it.

## Add or change a mark

1. Masters are in `shared/marks/` (`mark/`, `tools/`, `techworx/mark/`) with the spec in `shared/marks/marks.spec.json`. They are source files; edit them deliberately and diff the result.
2. Follow `docs/brand/principles/shared.md`: one cut (40 regular, 64 small), corner radius 12 (7 on sharp points, concave sharp), keyline 448, optical size target, small master rebuilt heavier, dark-mode irradiation offset.
3. Generators are in `shared/scripts/`. Every path comes from `paths.py` (`MARKS`, `FONTS`, `OUT`, `CACHE`); do not hard-code a root. Setup and run order are in `shared/scripts/README.md`.
4. Scripts write to `packages/brand/build/` only, which is gitignored. Never write into `shared/marks` from a script; copy a result in by hand once you have checked it.
5. Run the spec pipeline in order (`compare.py`, `v2build.py`, `specs.py`, `small_mark.py`, `specs_html.py`) and diff `build/mark-specs/marks.spec.json` against the committed one by hand. The committed spec is never overwritten.
6. Check light and dark side by side at 16, 32 and 64px against a neighbouring mark.

## Generated: do not hand-edit or commit

Everything under `packages/brand/build/`, `.pkl` caches, `mark-specs.html`, reference PNGs, construction SVGs, social cards and exported mark files. Change the source or the script and regenerate. `shared/scripts/github/about/plan.py --apply` edits live GitHub repos; do not run it without being asked.

## Checks that must pass

- `cd packages/brand && npx vitest run`
- `npx oxlint` and `npx oxfmt --check .` in the package
- Spec pipeline completes offline (the `github/` renders also need Chrome)
- Both themes of any mark you changed, viewed side by side

## Claude design system artifact

The Orin DX and techworx.dev design system artifacts are not synced from this package yet; syncing is manual and not automated. Today the library prose is newer than the artifacts in places (Orin layout values, voice rules), and the artifacts carry content with no source here (cover, component previews, links, `lastChange` history). When syncing is set up: write the index last, keep `createdOnFiles` and the asset records, and note that `editing: "code"` makes the page read-only and replaces every file on each sync. Components are the real Astro ones in `packages/components`; do not move the hand-built artifact bundle here.

The source `tokens.json` stays complete because Panda reads it. `shared/scripts/stage_artifact.py` stages a fitted derived copy for the artifact (aliases resolved, role families merged, 12 families, 60 tokens each) and lists anything it cannot represent under `notRepresented` in `upload-manifest.json`; today only the ten `roleStep` duplicates. Never trim the source to fit the artifact, and run `npx vitest run` (`test/artifactFit.test.ts`) after a token change.

## Where history lives

The old library is `~/Projects/orin-dx-site/brand`. It is read-only history: explorations, renders, backups, hand-built component bundle, static brand books. Nothing here depends on it at runtime, and nothing in it should be edited. The historical decisions log is copied to `docs/brand/README.md`.
